---
/**
 * SeoulMarkets privacy notice (`/privacy`).
 *
 * 2026-11-28 rewrite (boss: review GDPR and CCPA and apply them).
 * The August page said "no accounts, no payment, no ads". By November the site had accounts, API keys,
 * PayPal checkout, trial requests, a newsletter list, comments and AdSense, so the page was simply wrong.
 * This version is written against GDPR Art. 13 and Art. 14 and the CCPA privacy-policy contents
 * (Civ. Code s.1798.130(a)(5), regulations s.7011).
 *
 * Rules for whoever edits this next:
 *   - Do not state anything the site does not do. If a feature is added that touches personal data,
 *     change this page in the same commit.
 *   - The measurement ID and the linked-domain list come from Analytics.astro, never typed by hand.
 *   - The region and Global Privacy Control behaviour described here is implemented in PrivacyGate.astro.
 *   - Internal basis documents live in docs/privacy/.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { 측정ID, 잇는곳 } from '../components/Analytics.astro';
import { PUBLISHER, SITE_URL } from '../consts';

const MAIL = 'admin@klifedesign.net';
const UPDATED = '28 November 2026';
const TITLE = 'Privacy notice';
const DESC = 'What personal data SeoulMarkets handles, why, who receives it, how long it is kept and how to use '
  + 'your rights under GDPR and CCPA, including if your name appears in one of our datasets.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  url: `${SITE_URL}/privacy`,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'SeoulMarkets', url: SITE_URL },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: PUBLISHER.legalName, email: MAIL },
};
---

<Base title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Last updated {UPDATED}. This page says what personal data we handle, why, who else receives it,
    how long we keep it and how to ask us about it. It covers seoulmarkets.com, its API and the
    datasets we license.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      The controller is <b>{PUBLISHER.legalName}</b> ({PUBLISHER.address}), a company registered in
      the Republic of Korea. For anything on this page write to
      <a href={`mailto:${MAIL}`}>{MAIL}</a>. A person reads that inbox. We have not appointed a data
      protection officer because the law does not require one for what we do.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect from you, and why</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What</th><th>Why, and legal basis (GDPR Art. 6)</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>You create an account</td>
          <td>Email address, a one-way hash of your password, the list of what you bought</td>
          <td>To give you access to what you bought. Contract (6(1)(b)).</td>
          <td>Until you ask us to delete the account</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>You get an API key</td>
          <td>A one-way hash of your email and of the key, the plan, request counts</td>
          <td>To authenticate calls and apply plan limits. Contract (6(1)(b)).</td>
          <td>Until the key is revoked or you ask for deletion</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>You pay</td>
          <td>PayPal order ID, amount, product, time, the email on the order. We never see or store card numbers.</td>
          <td>To deliver the purchase and keep accounts. Contract (6(1)(b)) and legal obligation (6(1)(c)).</td>
          <td>Five years, as Korean commerce law requires for payment records</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>You request a trial or write to us</td>
          <td>Email address and whatever you tell us (organisation, role, what you need)</td>
          <td>To answer you. Steps before a contract (6(1)(b)) or our legitimate interest in answering enquiries (6(1)(f)).</td>
          <td>Two years after the last message, or until you ask for deletion</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>You join the mailing list</td>
          <td>Email address, the time, the page you signed up from</td>
          <td>To send what you asked for. Consent (6(1)(a)); withdraw at any time by replying "stop".</td>
          <td>Until you unsubscribe</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>You post a comment or vote</td>
          <td>The display name and text you type. No IP address, cookie or session ID is stored with it.</td>
          <td>To show the comment. Legitimate interest (6(1)(f)).</td>
          <td>Until you ask us to remove it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>You open a page</td>
          <td>
            Our server counts visits. It does not store your IP address. It stores a one-way hash that
            changes every day, so the same visitor cannot be followed from one day to the next. Attack
            protection reads IP addresses in memory; when it blocks an address it writes a partly
            masked form of it to the server log.
          </td>
          <td>To count visitors and block attacks. Legitimate interest (6(1)(f)).</td>
          <td>Daily hashes and counts are kept as statistics; they cannot be turned back into an IP address. Server logs: as long as the hosting provider retains them</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      You are not obliged to give us any of this. Without an email address we cannot create an account
      or deliver a purchase. We make no automated decisions about you and do no profiling.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2>Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Three third-party services can run on this site: <b>Google Analytics 4</b> (measurement ID
      <code>{측정ID}</code>, shared across {잇는곳.join(', ')} so that a visit moving between them is
      counted once), <b>Naver Analytics</b>, and <b>Google AdSense</b> advertising with the Google
      preferred-source button. They set cookies and tell Google or Naver which page was opened, from
      roughly where, on what kind of device.
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, none of them is
      loaded.</b> We recognise this from your browser's time zone, without looking up your IP address.
      You will see the same pages without analytics or advertising cookies, so there is nothing to
      consent to and no banner.
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, none of them is loaded either</b>,
      wherever you are. We treat the signal as an opt-out.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Elsewhere you can still switch them off with your browser's tracking protection or Google's
      opt-out add-on. Nothing on the site breaks. When you sign in, the site keeps a sign-in token in
      your browser's local storage; it is needed for the account page to work and is removed when you
      sign out.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who receives personal data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Google</b> (Ireland and United States): analytics and advertising as described above, and Google Workspace, which carries our email.</li>
      <li><b>Naver</b> (Republic of Korea): analytics.</li>
      <li><b>PayPal</b>: payments. PayPal acts as its own controller under its own privacy notice.</li>
      <li><b>Cloudtype</b> (Republic of Korea): hosting.</li>
      <li><b>Cloudflare</b> (United States): object storage for account, key and order records, encrypted in transit.</li>
      <li><b>RapidAPI</b>: only if you subscribe through RapidAPI, which then handles your account and billing under its own notice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data and we do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.
      We disclose it to authorities only when the law compels us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Transfers outside your country</h2>
    <p>
      We are in the Republic of Korea, which the European Commission and the United Kingdom recognise
      as providing adequate protection. When our providers process data in the United States, the
      transfer relies on the provider's certification under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework or on
      standard contractual clauses in the provider's data processing terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="named-in-data">
    <h2>If your name appears in one of our datasets</h2>
    <p>
      Some datasets we license (company ownership filings, officer and major-shareholder filings and
      workforce filings) contain the names of company officers and of shareholders who were legally
      required to file. This notice is given under GDPR Art. 14. Writing to each person named is not
      practicable, so we publish it here instead (Art. 14(5)(b)).
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source:</b> public regulatory disclosure systems only: DART (Financial Supervisory Service, Korea), EDINET (Financial Services Agency, Japan), the Taiwan Stock Exchange and the ADX and DFM exchanges in the UAE. We did not obtain the data from you.</li>
      <li><b>What:</b> name, role or relationship to the company, shareholding and changes in it, and for some officers the compensation the company disclosed. Nothing beyond what the filing itself made public. No contact details, no national ID numbers, no special-category data.</li>
      <li><b>Why:</b> so that investors and researchers can read mandatory corporate disclosures in English. Legal basis: our legitimate interest and that of our customers in the transparency of listed companies (Art. 6(1)(f)), which is the purpose the disclosure laws themselves serve.</li>
      <li><b>Who receives it:</b> customers who license the datasets, such as asset managers, researchers and software developers.</li>
      <li><b>How long:</b> for as long as the filing remains part of the public record.</li>
      <li><b>Your rights:</b> you can ask for a copy of what we hold about you, ask us to correct it against the filing, or object. If you object and we have no overriding reason, we remove your name from future releases within one month.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="rights">
    <h2>Your rights, and how to use them</h2>
    <p>
      Wherever you live, you can ask us to tell you what we hold about you, give you a copy, correct
      it, delete it, restrict or stop a use you object to, hand it to you in a portable format, or
      withdraw a consent you gave. Write to <a href={`mailto:${MAIL}`}>{MAIL}</a> from the address
      concerned, or tell us enough to find the record. There is no fee and no form.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>We acknowledge every request within 10 business days.</li>
      <li>We answer within one month. If a request is complex we may take up to two more months and will tell you why within the first month.</li>
      <li>We will not treat you differently for using these rights.</li>
      <li>If you are in the EEA, the UK or Switzerland you can also complain to your data protection authority. In Korea the authority is the Personal Information Protection Commission.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="california">
    <h2>California residents (CCPA)</h2>
    <p>
      We are below the thresholds that make a company a "business" under the California Consumer
      Privacy Act, and we are not a data broker under California law. We give California residents the
      same rights anyway.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Categories collected in the last 12 months:</b> identifiers (email address, hashed credentials); commercial information (what you bought); internet activity (pages opened, through the analytics described above); and the text of messages you sent us. Sources and purposes are in the table at the top of this page.</li>
      <li><b>Sold or shared:</b> none. We do not sell personal information and do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising. We honour Global Privacy Control signals.</li>
      <li><b>Sensitive personal information:</b> we do not collect it.</li>
      <li><b>Your rights:</b> to know, to delete, to correct, to opt out of sale or sharing, and not to be discriminated against for using them. Write to <a href={`mailto:${MAIL}`}>{MAIL}</a>; an authorised agent may write on your behalf with your signed permission. We confirm receipt within 10 business days and respond within 45 days.</li>
      <li><b>Names in our datasets:</b> these come from mandatory public filings and are publicly available information. See the section above if your name appears.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Passwords and API keys are stored only as one-way hashes. Traffic is encrypted. Access to stored
      records is limited to the people who run the service. If a breach
      affecting your data occurs we will notify the competent authority within 72 hours where the law
      requires it, and you without undue delay if the risk to you is high.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If what we do changes, this page changes on the same day and the date at the top moves.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="back">
    <a href="/about">How we make these numbers</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/terms">Terms</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/">Front page</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.25; margin: 1.2rem 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.4rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  p { font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 .9rem; }
  .note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  ul { padding-left: 1.15rem; font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0; }
  li { margin: 0 0 .45rem; }
  code { font-size: .9em; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 .9rem; display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
  th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: .5rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent); min-width: 9rem; }
  th { font-weight: 600; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .back a { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
